{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1344948-invoking-a-path","id":1344948,"title":"Invoking a path","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-31T08:21:37-07:00","id":1344948,"title":"Invoking a path","content":"What does invoking a path do? Is it only used to activate a Twist of Fate? It is mentioned in several places but I cannot seem to find a precise definition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25751-thidlemump","name":"Thidlemump","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T11:51:27-07:00","id":1345010,"title":"","content":"On page 99 in Origin, it is stated that you can invoke a path to access something that is related to your path. Like if you\u2019re a cop you have access to the police station. Paths can also be invoked to give you 2 dice to any roll connected to it. Paths can also be invoked once a session to call upon a connection or contact. Hopes this helps!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T15:54:03-07:00","id":1345086,"title":"","content":"Technically you can call up a Path for Contacts more than once per session, you've just strained the connection and you gotta do them a solid before you can use it again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b